# Course 1 · Agentic AI
## Agent design & theory
### Agent anatomy
- LLM: the brain, only writes text
- Tools: functions your code runs
- Instructions: the system prompt
- Memory: chat history, long-term
- Orchestration: the loop around it
### CoT vs. ReAct
- CoT: reason in steps, one call
- ReAct: reason + act with tools
### Model choice
- Capability · cost · latency
- Decompose → cheaper model
## Core prompting
### Prompt components
- Role / persona
- Task
- Output format
- Examples
- Context
### Chain-of-Thought
- Written steps = working memory
### Refinement
- Change one component at a time
- Compare on the same inputs
## Advanced patterns
### ReAct loop
- THINK → ACT → OBSERVE
- Two exits: final answer, step limit
### Prompt chaining
- Output of one step → input of the next
- Workflow (code decides) vs. agent (model decides)
### Gate checks
- Format · content · logic
- Pydantic contracts
- Rules in code, fail closed
### Feedback loops
- Tests are the spec
- Full report back, iteration limit
- Monitor every iteration
`.trim();

